WEBVTT

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.710
6th Division Heavy Cruiser Kako

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.940
6th Division Heavy Cruiser Furutaka

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.320
6th Division Heavy Cruiser Kinugasa

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:46.080
18th Division Light Cruiser Tenryu

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:56.630
6th Division Heavy Cruiser Aoba

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:13.270
8th Fleet Flagship Heavy Cruiser Chokai

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.990
This is a standard night battle.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.070
We'll go in expecting certain victory.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.320
All hands, stay calm and collected,

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.170
and give it your all.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.290
Fleet, speed up!

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:50.810
"Kantai Collection: The Movie"

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.330
Impending combat.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:55.100
Prepare for night battle.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.110
Enemy ship detected.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.890
30 degrees starboard.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:28.840
It's a destroyer.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.630
Target port side.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:22.030
Main batteries.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.860
Take careful aim.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:32.160
Open fire!

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.910
Why, you!

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.580
Lucky!

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.640
Enemy to port.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:52.660
Tenryu!

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.500
Furutaka and the rest are lagging behind.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.910
It seems those enemies haven't noticed us.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.880
Open fire!

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:57.200
We'll proceed to the enemy's base

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.540
and sink their transport fleet.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:54.700
Hey, Chokai...

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:56.730
I'm fine.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:11.150
What?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.790
This voice...

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.410
What's going on? The water's...

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.750
Hey, look over there...

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.430
We're nearly at the Shortland Islands.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.210
I wonder if everybody's doing okay.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:17.970
Hiryu, may I call back
the first shift air-support squadron?

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:20.430
All right.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.950
Prepare for landing, Soryu squadron.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:28.020
Buin's stationed flying corps will take over
air support for the returning 8th Fleet.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.270
All done!

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.940
Ryujo, are your ASW aircraft good to go?

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.610
They sure are.

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:38.740
I'll send 'em out one more time.

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.580
Man, the report said as much,

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.500
but the ocean really has turned crimson, eh?

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:58.860
Ryujo, with this formation,
enemy submarines can't approach us, right?

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:00.610
Obviously!

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:04.400
Also, Fubuki, don't these crimson waters bother you?

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.810
It seems the Solomon waters are even redder.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:09.850
What the...?!

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:18.940
What is this sound?

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:20.470
A voice?

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:24.780
What's wrong, Fubuki?

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:36.860
Don't worry. It's all right.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.570
Fubuki! Yudachi!

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:05.000
Mutsuki.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.160
Where? Where is she?!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:12.200
She's undergoing a damage assessment.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:13.080
Damage?!

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:14.890
Like, she's fine.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:16.500
It's, like, just in case.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:17.880
Oh...

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.690
Kisaragi...?

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:38.470
...tsuki...

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:03.840
Mutsuki...?

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:11.180
I'm back.

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:18.220
I...

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.750
Welcome back...

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:24.210
Welcome back!

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:27.990
Mutsuki.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.620
I'm so glad.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.000
But how'd this happen?

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:39.250
Kisaragi.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:41.630
Akagi!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:44.120
I hate to interrupt your joyful reunion,

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:47.090
but you should report to Secretary Nagato.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.080
Right.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:56.560
Mutsuki-Class Destroyer, Kisaragi,
reporting back.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:03.430
Good.

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:08.620
Unfortunately, the Admiral's out heading operations
with the Northern Fleet in Central waters.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.620
I'll let him know.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:11.910
Thank you very much.

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:14.030
I'm so glad you're back.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:18.510
I have lots of things to ask you,
but get some rest today.

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:20.620
I will, thank you.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:24.410
If you'll excuse me.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:33.880
There's no doubting it.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:40.810
I hereby designate this a Category D case.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:45.820
Until told otherwise,
everything regarding it is top secret.

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:50.570
But what are we gonna do?

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.370
Bucky and the rest don't know anything.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.620
But we can't quarantine her...

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:58.450
This won't be easy to deal with.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.400
How about some curry?

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:13.990
Welcome.

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:15.000
For two?

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:17.390
Would you like some special roast beef?

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.790
I'm Secretary Ship Nagato.

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:32.100
Thank you all for coming to Shortland Isles,
our base for the Solomon Island front lines.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:34.320
And, to the 8th Fleet,

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:39.470
which carried out a night raid on the enemy's
Solomon base and sank their transport ships...

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:40.810
You did brilliantly.

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:41.970
You have my gratitude.

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:45.000
It's all thanks to the 6th Division
and the rest of the fleet.

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:50.330
Eat and drink to your heart's content tonight.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:51.230
Cheers.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:53.350
Cheers!

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:55.070
You did great.

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:55.680
Oh, please.

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.050
So good!

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:02.440
Mamiya, your new anmitsu recipe is great!

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.120
Like!

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:06.260
It's, like, my tongue is melting!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.830
Oh, right.

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:11.740
We should take some to Kisaragi.

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:14.550
How's she doing?

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.310
She seemed fine,

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:19.450
but they said to let her rest, just in case.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:20.580
Oh.

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:23.540
Let's all go visit her later, then.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:25.060
Yeah.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.890
Roast beef!

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:31.920
You know what I think?

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:35.090
Oh, sweet. Give me another.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:38.230
Is this Kobe beef?

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:41.210
Of course not. Right, Yamato?

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:44.010
Right, but it's tender and delicious.

00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:45.420
Help yourselves.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:48.040
Oh, man, I love how fizzy this is.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.230
So this is the famous Hotel Yamato soda pop.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:52.440
I am not a hotel!

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.760
A strange voice around Solomon Islands?

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:02.790
We totally heard it
in the Solomon waters up ahead.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.290
Right, Amatsukaze?

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.060
R-Right.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:10.310
But, you know, it may have just been the wind.

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:13.320
What? No way!

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:15.950
Many others heard that voice!

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.280
Really? That's kinda scary.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.380
Sounds like a ghost.

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:21.930
What kind of voice was it?

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:25.390
It sounded sort of like a girl's voice.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.950
A somewhat lonely voice...

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:29.270
Hey! So you did hear it!

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:33.340
Tenryu?

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:35.110
Wh-What?

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:37.720
Did you hear it?

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:39.430
O-Oh, uh...

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:42.300
It sounded like a witch of the ocean,

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:45.290
beckoning you somewhere far away.

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:47.980
Right, Tenryu?

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:49.580
Stop that!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:50.820
My, my.

00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:03.560
<i>Did I sink?</i>

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:08.020
<i>I sank...</i>

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:10.470
<i>But, Akagi,</i>

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:12.940
<i>so long as you're okay, it's fine.</i>

00:18:14.930 --> 00:18:16.500
<i>I'm going first.</i>

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:18.980
<i>I'll be waiting for you.</i>

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:34.950
<i>I want to go back.</i>

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:42.050
<i>Back to my rightful place.</i>

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:45.650
<i>Let me go.</i>

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:48.820
Hey.

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.560
Hey, come on.

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:57.360
Category D case, huh?

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.240
Secretary Nagato told me.

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:02.990
Don't mention it so casually.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:05.080
It's a top secret—

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.860
What will happen to her?

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:08.960
You know, right?

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:28.730
I... back...

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:31.750
Give... back...

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:35.060
I... back...

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:36.650
A voice?

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:38.760
Give... back...

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.670
Fubuki? Is something, like, wrong?

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:46.200
No, nothing.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.430
It's almost wakeup time.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:05.690
Wake her or she'll, like, get yelled at.

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:07.720
She can sleep a little while longer.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:09.600
I mean, she only just got back.

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:16.760
So cute.

00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:19.230
She's, like, entranced by Kisaragi.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.670
Can you blame her?

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:22.450
She waited so long for her.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.160
Huh?

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:28.870
Good morning.

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:31.230
Mutsuki?

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:34.000
Yep. How are you feeling?

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.850
Pretty good.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:40.160
Good morning, Kisaragi.

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:41.050
Doing, like, okay?

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:43.770
Who are you?

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:45.820
I'm Fubuki.

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:49.020
Did you, like, forget about us?

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:50.340
Fubuki?

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:53.120
Don't worry!

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.980
I'm sure it's just the fatigue talking!

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:56.820
Y-Yeah...

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:02.490
And you haven't heard the voice since?

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:06.530
No. But I felt like I was being drawn in.

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.250
What do you think?

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:12.760
Other Fleet Girls have reported
hearing a similar voice.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:17.050
While it could be some kind of local phenomenon...

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:18.460
How does it look?

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:26.930
Well, I've mapped the locations where scouts and
Fleet Girls on missions reported hearing the voice.

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:29.060
Have a look.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:36.940
It's totally concentric.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.860
So the center of the circle is the source?

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:42.940
Ironbottom Sound...

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.380
Also known as Savo Sound,

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:49.660
a channel where lots of ships once sank.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:51.250
Right.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:53.290
We should probably investigate.

00:21:55.890 --> 00:21:57.080
Big trouble!

00:21:57.870 --> 00:21:58.900
What's wrong?

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.460
What happened here?

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:13.390
Nagato.

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:16.600
Uh, Kisaragi suddenly...

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:24.780
I...

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.520
I...

00:22:28.230 --> 00:22:30.760
It's okay. It's all right.

00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:33.900
You're just panicked right now, aren't you?

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:35.810
But...

00:22:35.810 --> 00:22:36.970
Don't worry.

00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:39.380
What is it?

00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:41.750
Well...

00:22:48.190 --> 00:22:49.450
Secretary Nagato.

00:22:54.240 --> 00:22:55.680
I'll tell them.

00:22:57.380 --> 00:23:00.190
No, if anyone should, it's me—

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:02.020
Please, let me.

00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:07.050
Very well.

00:23:07.050 --> 00:23:08.020
Thank you.

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:22.520
You know...

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:30.230
I once heard a rumor that said
there's a carrier with post-sinking memories.

00:23:31.830 --> 00:23:33.970
Why aren't you saying anything?

00:23:40.690 --> 00:23:41.720
Right.

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:45.240
Maybe it'd be a good idea to tell you, too.

00:23:59.760 --> 00:24:01.350
How are you feeling?

00:24:02.980 --> 00:24:05.680
Here, I brought you food.

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:07.930
You didn't eat much yesterday, either.

00:24:13.220 --> 00:24:15.830
Did she, like, always have a bruise there?

00:24:20.870 --> 00:24:22.840
Say, Mutsuki.

00:24:23.990 --> 00:24:27.020
Can I really stay here?

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:28.860
Kisaragi?

00:24:29.310 --> 00:24:30.830
What are you talking about?

00:24:30.830 --> 00:24:32.570
Of course you can!

00:24:32.570 --> 00:24:35.530
You've always been with us!

00:24:35.530 --> 00:24:39.830
But, every now and then,
my mind wanders someplace else.

00:24:40.530 --> 00:24:43.010
I try to return,

00:24:43.010 --> 00:24:45.830
but the distance keeps growing,

00:24:45.830 --> 00:24:47.940
and I go further into a dark place...

00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:49.930
I sink further into it.

00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:54.150
As much as I don't want to,
as much as it scares me,

00:24:54.150 --> 00:24:57.970
I end up feeling like I have to go.

00:24:59.470 --> 00:25:00.890
What are you saying?

00:25:00.890 --> 00:25:02.910
That can't be!

00:25:02.910 --> 00:25:06.940
All those scary nightmares
are putting those thoughts in your head!

00:25:06.940 --> 00:25:09.150
That's what I wanted to believe!

00:25:09.150 --> 00:25:13.180
But I started firing unconsciously today!

00:25:13.780 --> 00:25:16.530
If this keeps up, I'll attack you all!

00:25:16.530 --> 00:25:18.410
Like I said, that was...

00:25:19.160 --> 00:25:21.670
I'm so scared!

00:25:36.260 --> 00:25:38.250
I bet it's just the fatigue talking.

00:25:38.250 --> 00:25:40.170
I mean, she's been through a lot.

00:25:40.170 --> 00:25:42.440
You said, like, the same thing before.

00:25:43.060 --> 00:25:43.810
But...

00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:46.280
Come in.

00:25:47.990 --> 00:25:48.980
Akagi?

00:25:49.650 --> 00:25:51.640
How's Kisaragi?

00:25:51.640 --> 00:25:54.380
She just fell asleep.

00:25:54.380 --> 00:25:55.400
I see.

00:25:59.680 --> 00:26:00.790
We need to talk.

00:26:04.630 --> 00:26:05.960
What do you mean?

00:26:06.500 --> 00:26:08.040
Exactly what I said.

00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:10.880
Kisaragi can't stay here.

00:26:10.880 --> 00:26:14.010
But why? She's one of us!

00:26:14.010 --> 00:26:16.720
A Fleet girl, just like us!

00:26:16.720 --> 00:26:18.070
We know that.

00:26:18.630 --> 00:26:20.900
But she sank.

00:26:21.410 --> 00:26:23.710
She's not who she used to be.

00:26:23.710 --> 00:26:26.180
What? You're wrong!

00:26:26.180 --> 00:26:28.160
But she came back.

00:26:28.160 --> 00:26:33.610
She looked for us and finally found
her way back to Mutsuki.

00:26:33.990 --> 00:26:40.870
Indeed. There's no doubt that she had
a strong desire to come back to us.

00:26:40.870 --> 00:26:42.620
It's the undeniable truth.

00:26:42.620 --> 00:26:46.160
But the fact that she sank won't change.

00:26:46.800 --> 00:26:50.630
She'll eventually become an Abyssal Vessel.

00:26:51.020 --> 00:26:52.750
Abyssal...?

00:26:52.750 --> 00:26:54.300
What do you mean?

00:26:54.740 --> 00:26:56.880
It's as Kaga said.

00:26:56.880 --> 00:26:58.310
If left alone—

00:26:58.310 --> 00:27:01.800
No, it's likely that no matter what we do,

00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:05.890
she'll eventually become an Abyssal Vessel.

00:27:06.890 --> 00:27:08.620
What?

00:27:08.620 --> 00:27:11.850
Are you saying that's a fake Kisaragi?!

00:27:12.190 --> 00:27:13.110
No.

00:27:13.400 --> 00:27:15.070
She's the real deal.

00:27:15.070 --> 00:27:16.810
One of us.

00:27:16.810 --> 00:27:19.740
The second Mutsuki-Class Destroyer, Kisaragi.

00:27:20.700 --> 00:27:26.730
She vanished into the depths of the ocean
while wanting to come back, to come home.

00:27:27.650 --> 00:27:32.750
With some Fleet girls, that strong desire,
sorrow, and frustration

00:27:32.750 --> 00:27:36.670
makes them transform into Abyssal Vessels.

00:27:37.590 --> 00:27:46.100
And, actually, a certain Fleet Girl has
faint memories of fighting us as an Abyssal Vessel.

00:27:46.590 --> 00:27:47.890
Isn't that right, Kaga?

00:27:49.560 --> 00:27:53.800
Lingering sorrow, frustration, and regret.

00:27:54.980 --> 00:27:56.570
Me, of all people.

00:27:56.570 --> 00:28:01.820
And oppressive memories of unbearable pain.

00:28:02.200 --> 00:28:04.120
"I want to go home. I want to make it happen.

00:28:04.480 --> 00:28:05.710
I can do this.

00:28:05.710 --> 00:28:07.240
This can't be."

00:28:07.580 --> 00:28:09.370
I take those emotions

00:28:09.680 --> 00:28:12.020
and throw them at
the living beings in front of me.

00:28:13.350 --> 00:28:15.480
They are sad, painful memories.

00:28:15.480 --> 00:28:18.860
Does that mean the Abyssal Fleet...

00:28:18.860 --> 00:28:21.220
The enemies we're fighting...

00:28:22.220 --> 00:28:24.840
...used to be just like us?

00:28:25.350 --> 00:28:27.910
It's not out of the question.

00:28:27.910 --> 00:28:30.020
Haven't you ever felt it yourself?

00:28:30.500 --> 00:28:33.930
A modicum of emotion in Abyssal Vessels?

00:28:34.460 --> 00:28:36.360
Something that resonates within you?

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:40.250
That's absurd!

00:28:41.150 --> 00:28:46.320
After we sink, parts of us
turn into Abyssal Vessels

00:28:46.680 --> 00:28:49.620
and try to come home to us.

00:28:52.330 --> 00:28:56.920
Is that what we're fighting?

00:28:57.460 --> 00:28:59.610
That's, like, meaningless!

00:28:59.610 --> 00:29:02.470
Does this war have any point at all?

00:29:03.310 --> 00:29:05.270
It does have a point.

00:29:08.910 --> 00:29:10.680
The fact that Kaga is here with us—

00:29:11.460 --> 00:29:15.820
that a Fleet Girl with memories of
being an Abyssal Vessel is here—

00:29:15.820 --> 00:29:19.730
means she could turn back into a Fleet Girl.

00:29:21.120 --> 00:29:22.990
But how?

00:29:22.990 --> 00:29:24.150
I don't know.

00:29:24.530 --> 00:29:28.710
But what if, just as Fleet Girls sink
and become Abyssal Vessels,

00:29:29.300 --> 00:29:34.970
Abyssal Vessels sink and become Fleet Girls?

00:29:35.970 --> 00:29:37.940
If that is indeed what happens...

00:29:46.230 --> 00:29:50.850
But doesn't that mean the war will never end?

00:29:51.350 --> 00:29:56.060
Fleet Girls sunk by Abyssal Vessels
will become Abyssal Vessels,

00:29:56.060 --> 00:30:00.430
and Abyssal Vessels sunk by Fleet Girls
will turn back into Fleet Girls...

00:30:00.430 --> 00:30:02.050
No, you're wrong.

00:30:02.780 --> 00:30:06.030
If none of us sink,

00:30:06.030 --> 00:30:08.740
and we sink the entire Abyssal Fleet,

00:30:09.680 --> 00:30:12.450
I see! If we could do that...

00:30:12.930 --> 00:30:15.750
Right. That's our only hope.

00:30:15.750 --> 00:30:21.420
The only way we Fleet Girls can end this war.

00:30:22.050 --> 00:30:25.840
That's why we cannot afford to sink.

00:30:40.600 --> 00:30:43.040
What about Kisaragi, then?

00:30:43.040 --> 00:30:45.050
What will happen to Kisaragi?

00:30:45.920 --> 00:30:48.860
If we are to save her...

00:30:51.410 --> 00:30:56.950
...sinking her as an Abyssal Vessel
is the only way to do it.

00:31:00.620 --> 00:31:02.540
That's horrible!

00:31:04.540 --> 00:31:08.470
That's just way too cruel!

00:31:26.910 --> 00:31:32.360
Message from 2nd CarDiv Flagship Hiryu,
patrolling the northern Solomon waters.

00:31:34.910 --> 00:31:35.410
Read it out.

00:31:35.800 --> 00:31:41.040
"From Hiryu of the 2nd Carrier Division.
To Southern Waters HQ Secretary Nagato.

00:31:41.620 --> 00:31:48.110
Spotted enemy fleet with multiple task forces
in the South Pacific, Northern Solomon waters."

00:31:48.110 --> 00:31:48.840
What?

00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:53.690
"Each task force is in circular formation,
with a Carrier Princess at the core,

00:31:53.690 --> 00:31:57.890
escorted by several T-Class Battleships
and S-Class Cruisers."

00:31:57.890 --> 00:31:59.640
That sounds like insane numbers.

00:31:59.640 --> 00:32:02.330
A large fleet of carrier battle groups, huh?

00:32:02.880 --> 00:32:04.520
Follow-up from 2nd CarDiv's Hiryu.

00:32:05.110 --> 00:32:08.150
"Taking command of air battle.

00:32:08.150 --> 00:32:10.320
Sending out aerial attack squad."

00:32:10.320 --> 00:32:14.490
That's very like Hiryu,
but her division's outnumbered.

00:32:14.990 --> 00:32:17.640
Tell her to retreat after landing some hits.

00:32:17.640 --> 00:32:19.100
We'll cover their retreat.

00:32:19.100 --> 00:32:23.610
Have Shokaku and Zuikaku of the 5th CarDiv
sortie at once and act as their rear guard.

00:32:23.610 --> 00:32:24.330
Roger.

00:32:24.330 --> 00:32:30.120
But tell them to withdraw at full speed
as soon as they pick up the 2nd CarDiv.

00:32:30.120 --> 00:32:30.670
Right?

00:32:32.240 --> 00:32:33.300
Correct.

00:32:35.910 --> 00:32:38.720
Message from Kongo's squad,
surveying Ironbottom Sound.

00:32:39.700 --> 00:32:42.180
They've reached the target survey area.

00:32:46.610 --> 00:32:48.700
As Nagato feared,

00:32:48.700 --> 00:32:50.950
this is a bit of a problem, I must say.

00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:55.060
The ocean changed color?

00:32:58.390 --> 00:33:03.450
The weird voice coming from Ironbottom Sound
is gradually spreading,

00:33:03.450 --> 00:33:06.830
and the water's changing color along with it.

00:33:06.830 --> 00:33:08.260
Changing color?

00:33:08.720 --> 00:33:11.630
I think the 8th Fleet reported that, too.

00:33:12.760 --> 00:33:14.110
Nagato.

00:33:14.110 --> 00:33:16.260
Thank you. Leave it there.

00:33:20.270 --> 00:33:24.150
The ecosystem has been destroyed
in the discolored waters.

00:33:24.150 --> 00:33:24.810
What's more...

00:33:25.810 --> 00:33:27.310
Equipment gets damaged?

00:33:27.310 --> 00:33:28.060
Yes.

00:33:28.420 --> 00:33:33.070
Sister and I took minor equipment damage.

00:33:33.070 --> 00:33:37.500
The damage gets worse
the longer a ship sails those waters.

00:33:37.500 --> 00:33:41.790
There's no doubt that
the discoloration is causing it somehow.

00:33:42.350 --> 00:33:44.870
So if we stay there too long,

00:33:44.870 --> 00:33:47.910
we might be unable to use our equipment?

00:33:49.880 --> 00:33:52.700
Yamato of BatDiv 1 reporting. Sorry I'm late.

00:33:52.700 --> 00:33:55.720
Akagi and Kaga of CarDiv 1 reporting in, too.

00:33:58.990 --> 00:34:01.680
The discolored area is expanding?

00:34:01.680 --> 00:34:02.670
Yes.

00:34:02.670 --> 00:34:08.090
Going by Type 0 Observer Seaplane reports
and latest observation results,

00:34:08.690 --> 00:34:11.570
it's growing by this much in one day.

00:34:12.150 --> 00:34:13.530
That's pretty fast.

00:34:14.990 --> 00:34:19.490
If it maintains this rate,
then in three days and seven hours...

00:34:22.850 --> 00:34:24.830
It'll reach this base in a few days?

00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:30.040
The estimated point of origin hasn't changed.

00:34:30.040 --> 00:34:31.800
It remains in Ironbottom Sound,

00:34:31.800 --> 00:34:34.400
here at Point Liquorice.

00:34:34.400 --> 00:34:35.480
Liquorice...

00:34:36.210 --> 00:34:39.000
Where we neutralized that Airfield Princess?

00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:41.610
Who dares wins! Catch and kill!

00:34:41.610 --> 00:34:43.240
That's our only choice!

00:34:43.240 --> 00:34:45.140
I'd like to agree, but...

00:34:45.780 --> 00:34:49.380
Worried about the carrier battle groups
the 2nd CarDiv encountered?

00:34:49.380 --> 00:34:50.150
Yes.

00:34:50.540 --> 00:34:53.660
They landed some hits on some of them,

00:34:53.660 --> 00:34:55.940
but a lot of fighters didn't return.

00:34:55.940 --> 00:34:59.860
They're currently restocking and redrilling.

00:35:00.230 --> 00:35:01.590
The 2nd CarDiv?

00:35:03.350 --> 00:35:06.040
How many carrier battle groups have we seen?

00:35:06.040 --> 00:35:10.790
More than six led by Carrier Princesses.

00:35:11.440 --> 00:35:12.270
Right here.

00:35:13.330 --> 00:35:17.000
Their estimated destination is...

00:35:18.240 --> 00:35:20.400
Ironbottom Sound.

00:35:20.400 --> 00:35:22.010
The voice's origin point?

00:35:22.570 --> 00:35:24.730
Just what is there?

00:35:25.430 --> 00:35:28.680
When will the enemy fleet get there?

00:35:28.680 --> 00:35:32.730
At their current speed, approx 58 hours.

00:35:32.730 --> 00:35:34.220
In three days?

00:35:34.220 --> 00:35:35.980
Yes. Less than three days, actually.

00:35:36.320 --> 00:35:37.610
What will we do?

00:35:37.610 --> 00:35:41.910
If that fleet gets there,
it'll be impossible to raid Ironbottom Sound.

00:35:41.910 --> 00:35:45.710
But if we rush blindly into the discolored waters,

00:35:45.710 --> 00:35:50.330
we could get damaged and maybe even
wiped out before we encounter the enemy.

00:35:58.710 --> 00:36:00.410
What do we, like, do?

00:36:00.410 --> 00:36:01.880
What, you ask?

00:36:01.880 --> 00:36:04.760
There's no way we can tell her.

00:36:04.760 --> 00:36:06.100
But, at this rate...

00:36:06.440 --> 00:36:09.230
Don't worry! It'll work out somehow!

00:36:09.230 --> 00:36:11.760
I mean, Kisaragi came back to us!

00:36:11.760 --> 00:36:14.650
She came back for us!

00:36:15.410 --> 00:36:19.960
She'd never become an Abyssal Vessel.

00:36:25.040 --> 00:36:28.220
I don't know how it works,

00:36:28.220 --> 00:36:33.670
but the Fleet Girls who sailed the discolored waters
have had their equipment damaged.

00:36:33.670 --> 00:36:34.790
I see.

00:36:34.790 --> 00:36:37.910
But the Special-Class Destroyer, Fubuki...

00:36:37.910 --> 00:36:39.130
Only she...

00:36:40.340 --> 00:36:41.460
Fubuki?

00:36:48.780 --> 00:36:51.380
Is Kisaragi in really bad shape?

00:36:51.380 --> 00:36:54.060
It's not like she's in "bad" shape, but...

00:36:58.110 --> 00:37:01.360
Are you tired, Fubuki?

00:37:01.360 --> 00:37:02.900
Lemme take a look!

00:37:02.900 --> 00:37:04.390
Growl!

00:37:04.390 --> 00:37:06.150
That tickles!

00:37:06.150 --> 00:37:07.320
S-Stop that!

00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:09.740
Where's the problem?

00:37:10.370 --> 00:37:12.660
There you are, Fubuki.

00:37:13.460 --> 00:37:14.580
Akagi!

00:37:16.130 --> 00:37:17.250
Aren't you having fun.

00:37:18.030 --> 00:37:20.340
Th-This isn't what it looks like!

00:37:23.620 --> 00:37:24.800
The equipment?

00:37:25.220 --> 00:37:29.590
Apparently, only yours took no damage at all.

00:37:29.590 --> 00:37:33.350
Huh? Was it only me?

00:37:34.020 --> 00:37:35.640
What about replying to the voice?

00:37:35.640 --> 00:37:37.560
Huh? Did someone do that?

00:37:38.150 --> 00:37:40.730
I was told that when you all heard the voice,

00:37:41.710 --> 00:37:43.940
you spoke to it as if to calm it down.

00:37:43.940 --> 00:37:45.890
Who, me?

00:37:46.380 --> 00:37:47.800
You don't remember?

00:37:49.790 --> 00:37:51.040
Fubuki.

00:37:51.040 --> 00:37:51.790
Yes?

00:37:52.140 --> 00:37:55.460
Which base were you stationed at before?

00:37:56.660 --> 00:37:59.050
Er, I think it was...

00:37:59.730 --> 00:38:00.630
Huh?

00:38:02.180 --> 00:38:04.350
When did you meet the Admiral?

00:38:04.350 --> 00:38:06.730
After I was assigned to the current base.

00:38:06.730 --> 00:38:08.710
That was the first time.

00:38:08.710 --> 00:38:10.030
Really?

00:38:10.030 --> 00:38:11.010
Yes.

00:38:11.360 --> 00:38:14.080
What division were you in at the last base?

00:38:14.080 --> 00:38:16.180
Who was the flagship of your torpedo squadron?

00:38:16.180 --> 00:38:19.720
U-Uh, I think it was...

00:38:19.720 --> 00:38:20.860
Um...

00:38:34.950 --> 00:38:36.290
I...

00:38:36.990 --> 00:38:40.250
...sinking her as an Abyssal Vessel

00:38:40.900 --> 00:38:42.500
is the only way to do it.

00:38:43.080 --> 00:38:48.130
I'm going to become an Abyssal Vessel?

00:38:48.690 --> 00:38:49.860
If this keeps up?

00:38:57.090 --> 00:38:57.900
No...

00:38:58.730 --> 00:39:00.290
No!

00:39:01.610 --> 00:39:04.270
No! No!

00:39:04.270 --> 00:39:06.530
Why can't I get it off?!

00:39:20.470 --> 00:39:21.210
Kisaragi!

00:39:28.430 --> 00:39:29.970
Kisaragi...

00:39:32.460 --> 00:39:33.550
Wait!

00:39:37.040 --> 00:39:40.020
I... I...

00:39:41.390 --> 00:39:43.310
Don't worry.

00:39:43.310 --> 00:39:46.730
I'll always be with you,

00:39:47.600 --> 00:39:48.940
no matter what.

00:39:49.870 --> 00:39:52.950
But... But I...

00:39:53.780 --> 00:39:55.400
Don't say another word.

00:39:57.460 --> 00:40:01.230
You don't have to worry about a thing.

00:40:01.230 --> 00:40:03.820
You went through so much all by yourself,

00:40:03.820 --> 00:40:05.650
and you finally came back.

00:40:06.370 --> 00:40:07.940
You did nothing wrong.

00:40:08.610 --> 00:40:09.970
Mutsuki...

00:40:10.400 --> 00:40:11.290
That's right.

00:40:11.920 --> 00:40:13.930
No matter what anyone says,

00:40:13.930 --> 00:40:15.720
no matter what happens,

00:40:16.240 --> 00:40:19.560
I'll always be with you!

00:40:19.560 --> 00:40:20.390
So please...

00:40:25.780 --> 00:40:27.020
Fubuki?

00:40:27.020 --> 00:40:27.730
Yes.

00:40:28.120 --> 00:40:30.940
Of the ships that sailed the discolored waters,

00:40:30.940 --> 00:40:35.030
only Fubuki's equipment didn't get damaged.

00:40:35.030 --> 00:40:44.710
Also, the voice from Ironbottom Sound
was first heard on the day she reached this base.

00:40:44.710 --> 00:40:48.000
We could dismiss it as a coincidence...

00:40:48.470 --> 00:40:51.840
But we can't deny the possibility of a link.

00:40:52.190 --> 00:40:56.780
As made clear in the Ironbottom Sound waters,

00:40:56.780 --> 00:41:01.940
it'd be natural to assume
she has something other Fleet Girls don't.

00:41:03.660 --> 00:41:05.150
What will you do?

00:41:05.150 --> 00:41:08.060
That's not reason enough to launch.

00:41:09.010 --> 00:41:10.070
But...

00:41:28.710 --> 00:41:31.620
What should I wish for?

00:41:36.840 --> 00:41:38.380
Yamato!

00:41:38.380 --> 00:41:39.510
What's the matter?

00:41:39.510 --> 00:41:41.420
What about you?

00:41:41.420 --> 00:41:43.930
Are you done with maintenance and resupply?

00:41:44.330 --> 00:41:45.000
Yes.

00:41:45.670 --> 00:41:48.020
Mind if I sit next to you?

00:41:49.110 --> 00:41:50.070
Sure.

00:42:02.670 --> 00:42:04.690
It's such a peaceful ocean.

00:42:04.690 --> 00:42:05.330
It is.

00:42:09.780 --> 00:42:10.810
Uh...

00:42:12.130 --> 00:42:15.760
Did you all know about it beforehand?

00:42:18.080 --> 00:42:20.120
I suppose you could say that.

00:42:21.880 --> 00:42:27.860
Do you think there's no escape
from this world and our war?

00:42:31.110 --> 00:42:34.440
The Abyssal Fleet we've been fighting is...

00:42:36.200 --> 00:42:38.910
When I think about that, it's too much.

00:42:40.480 --> 00:42:44.300
Why have we taken life as Fleet Girls?

00:42:44.300 --> 00:42:46.580
Why are we here? What is our purpose?

00:42:47.510 --> 00:42:51.250
Why were we born?

00:42:51.990 --> 00:42:56.310
"I want to protect my friends and my bonds.

00:42:56.310 --> 00:42:58.220
I want to tell them how I feel."

00:42:59.480 --> 00:43:02.580
Maybe that's why we're here.

00:43:04.950 --> 00:43:05.600
Yes.

00:43:06.240 --> 00:43:09.080
Our war does have meaning.

00:43:09.080 --> 00:43:12.760
Though our goal might be a really tough one,

00:43:13.250 --> 00:43:14.580
we can do it.

00:43:15.410 --> 00:43:18.360
Perhaps that is what you call "hope."

00:43:19.360 --> 00:43:20.560
Hope?

00:43:20.560 --> 00:43:21.160
Yes.

00:43:21.580 --> 00:43:23.070
Hope to protect everyone

00:43:23.570 --> 00:43:26.460
and end this war of ours.

00:43:56.930 --> 00:43:58.110
You've decided?

00:43:58.520 --> 00:43:59.330
Correct.

00:44:08.530 --> 00:44:11.560
The ships taking part have all gathered.

00:44:24.540 --> 00:44:30.600
We will hereby launch
an all-out operation to Solomon Islands.

00:44:30.600 --> 00:44:31.850
All right.

00:44:31.850 --> 00:44:33.260
Sister.

00:44:33.260 --> 00:44:34.600
Let's do this.

00:44:34.600 --> 00:44:35.870
I'm good to go.

00:44:35.870 --> 00:44:37.230
You can count on me.

00:44:38.960 --> 00:44:40.820
So we're going on the offensive?

00:44:40.820 --> 00:44:42.320
It'll be, like, a good challenge.

00:44:42.900 --> 00:44:43.920
Sis?

00:44:43.920 --> 00:44:45.500
We're finally going on the attack!

00:44:45.500 --> 00:44:46.660
A night battle!

00:44:48.080 --> 00:44:53.870
The ultimate objective of this operation is to
find the source of the growing discoloration

00:44:53.870 --> 00:44:59.630
in Ironbottom Sound, Solomon Islands,
and exterminate it.

00:45:00.260 --> 00:45:01.720
In the discolored waters,

00:45:01.720 --> 00:45:04.910
all life except the Abyssal Fleet dies out,

00:45:04.910 --> 00:45:08.140
and our equipment gets corroded and damaged.

00:45:08.720 --> 00:45:12.310
Carrying out the operation in this scenario
will be highly difficult.

00:45:12.670 --> 00:45:13.850
But, if ignored,

00:45:14.160 --> 00:45:15.940
the discolored area will keep expanding,

00:45:16.430 --> 00:45:20.110
and attacking the core of Ironbottom sound

00:45:20.110 --> 00:45:22.180
will become impossible forever.

00:45:22.940 --> 00:45:29.770
As such, all surface vessels stationed here
at Shotland Isles will go on the offensive.

00:45:29.770 --> 00:45:33.140
Know that this mission is extremely crucial.

00:45:33.140 --> 00:45:37.250
I'll now read out each fleet's roster and hierarchy.

00:45:37.570 --> 00:45:38.600
1st Fleet:

00:45:38.600 --> 00:45:40.640
Carrier Battle Group Flagships,

00:45:40.640 --> 00:45:43.590
1st CarDiv's Akagi and Kaga.

00:45:43.590 --> 00:45:47.070
5th CarDiv's Shokaku and Zuikaku.

00:45:47.070 --> 00:45:49.990
Escorted by 3rd BatDiv's Kongo...

00:45:52.660 --> 00:45:53.560
That is all!

00:45:53.950 --> 00:45:56.840
Mission details will be passed along later.

00:45:56.840 --> 00:45:59.250
All of you prepare to sortie!

00:46:02.940 --> 00:46:04.590
Is that all of it?

00:46:04.590 --> 00:46:06.400
Let's go over it again.

00:46:06.400 --> 00:46:07.070
Yeah.

00:46:07.070 --> 00:46:11.130
Type 3 and Armor-Piercing Shells, too!

00:46:11.130 --> 00:46:12.970
I'll strike from outside their range...

00:46:12.970 --> 00:46:16.290
You'd best be prepared for the worst.

00:46:16.290 --> 00:46:19.610
What? Are you saying I might sink?

00:46:19.610 --> 00:46:21.320
Try not to.

00:46:23.110 --> 00:46:25.310
But, even if I do sink,

00:46:25.310 --> 00:46:27.550
there's a chance I could come back, right?

00:46:27.990 --> 00:46:30.760
Never say something like that again.

00:46:33.090 --> 00:46:39.150
There are no words that can describe
that pain and suffering.

00:46:39.880 --> 00:46:41.310
You should...

00:46:41.730 --> 00:46:44.950
You should know that yourself, deep down.

00:46:53.240 --> 00:46:57.190
Me? Sortie as the main force's escort?

00:46:57.190 --> 00:46:58.950
I didn't see that coming.

00:46:58.950 --> 00:47:00.280
Good for you.

00:47:00.280 --> 00:47:01.040
Yeah.

00:47:01.040 --> 00:47:03.750
I'm happy I can be of use to everyone.

00:47:08.720 --> 00:47:11.010
I'll be back as soon as possible, okay?

00:47:13.230 --> 00:47:16.260
Don't worry. I'll definitely come back.

00:47:16.840 --> 00:47:19.500
I'll never leave you alone.

00:47:20.200 --> 00:47:20.980
Okay...

00:47:27.140 --> 00:47:29.020
Here we go!

00:47:29.020 --> 00:47:31.980
I'll show you what I'm made of!

00:47:31.980 --> 00:47:34.490
All right! It's time for a night battle!

00:47:34.490 --> 00:47:36.830
You're the vanguard, huh, Sendai?

00:47:36.830 --> 00:47:40.080
I'm leading the advance recon squad.

00:47:40.080 --> 00:47:42.520
We'll definitely open up a path for you,

00:47:42.520 --> 00:47:44.060
so you'd better charge right in!

00:47:44.060 --> 00:47:44.620
Got it.

00:47:44.620 --> 00:47:48.600
Sis, don't get too worked up and push it.

00:47:48.600 --> 00:47:50.110
Got it, Jintsu.

00:47:50.110 --> 00:47:51.440
Flowering 2nd Torpedo Squadron,

00:47:51.440 --> 00:47:53.760
take care of the main force for me.

00:47:53.760 --> 00:47:56.180
Of course. Leave it to me.

00:47:57.270 --> 00:47:58.840
Yamato.

00:47:58.840 --> 00:48:02.280
This is our first time in the same fleet.

00:48:02.280 --> 00:48:04.610
Yes. I'll be in your care.

00:48:08.150 --> 00:48:10.050
I want to go back.

00:48:10.690 --> 00:48:12.570
Give back....

00:48:14.200 --> 00:48:15.840
This voice...

00:48:15.840 --> 00:48:17.180
It's calling?

00:48:32.640 --> 00:48:35.380
Please be safe, everyone.

00:48:37.810 --> 00:48:39.100
Syncing clock.

00:48:39.500 --> 00:48:40.220
Five...

00:48:40.220 --> 00:48:41.420
Four...

00:48:41.420 --> 00:48:42.380
Three...

00:48:42.380 --> 00:48:43.340
Two...

00:48:43.340 --> 00:48:44.100
One...

00:48:44.100 --> 00:48:44.980
Now!

00:48:44.980 --> 00:48:46.230
Commence mission!

00:48:46.640 --> 00:48:48.550
The mission has begun!

00:48:48.550 --> 00:48:49.690
Fleets, move out!

00:48:50.820 --> 00:48:53.340
All ships, weigh anchor!

00:49:00.240 --> 00:49:03.740
3rd Fleet, the support unit, moving out!

00:49:03.740 --> 00:49:05.960
2nd Carrier Division, weigh anchor!

00:49:16.010 --> 00:49:20.470
1st Fleet, 1st CarDiv, Akagi, moving out!

00:49:20.470 --> 00:49:21.770
Likewise, Kaga—

00:49:21.770 --> 00:49:22.730
Hey, 1st CarDiv.

00:49:25.780 --> 00:49:27.860
Sorry about earlier.

00:49:28.990 --> 00:49:30.020
What?

00:49:30.020 --> 00:49:31.580
For what I said.

00:49:33.840 --> 00:49:35.860
The mission is already underway.

00:49:37.250 --> 00:49:38.310
Do your best.

00:49:40.310 --> 00:49:42.900
Kaga of 1st CarDiv sortieing.

00:49:46.850 --> 00:49:48.840
Let's follow suit.

00:49:48.840 --> 00:49:51.310
From the 5th CarDiv, Zuikaku!

00:49:51.310 --> 00:49:52.380
Shokaku!

00:49:52.380 --> 00:49:53.800
Weighing anchor!

00:49:57.070 --> 00:49:59.590
Fubuki, let's stay calm and do this.

00:49:59.590 --> 00:50:00.540
Yes.

00:50:04.750 --> 00:50:05.830
Mutsuki.

00:50:07.300 --> 00:50:09.260
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:50:09.730 --> 00:50:11.240
Fubuki.

00:50:12.020 --> 00:50:12.890
You're right.

00:50:14.980 --> 00:50:18.230
The 2nd Fleet's main force,
Hiei, Kirishima, Yamato,

00:50:18.230 --> 00:50:20.300
and the rest of the raid unit have moved out.

00:50:20.300 --> 00:50:22.490
The main raid force, huh?

00:50:22.490 --> 00:50:24.090
Will they be all right?

00:50:24.090 --> 00:50:26.950
Trust their experience and teamwork.

00:50:27.920 --> 00:50:30.330
We should take up defensive positions, too.

00:50:35.730 --> 00:50:37.730
Here's an outline of the mission.

00:50:37.730 --> 00:50:41.530
1st CarDiv's Akagi and Kaga
will lead a carrier battle group,

00:50:41.530 --> 00:50:42.720
the 1st Fleet.

00:50:43.130 --> 00:50:46.120
5th CarDiv's ships will deal with enemies.

00:50:46.120 --> 00:50:49.700
Kongo and Haruna will escort the fleet.

00:50:50.980 --> 00:50:56.650
This fleet will intercept the approaching enemy
reinforcements, the fleet of carrier battle groups,

00:50:56.650 --> 00:50:58.690
and divert it to the north.

00:50:59.660 --> 00:51:04.700
And flanking the 1st Fleet will be
the restructured Hiryu and Soryu from 2nd CarDiv,

00:51:05.060 --> 00:51:06.630
Light Carrier Ryujo,

00:51:06.630 --> 00:51:08.970
Aviation Cruisers Suzuya and Kumano,

00:51:08.970 --> 00:51:10.170
a Heavy Cruiser Division,

00:51:10.170 --> 00:51:13.080
Light Cruiser Naka and her 4th Desron.

00:51:13.080 --> 00:51:14.750
That'll be the 3rd Fleet, the support unit.

00:51:16.080 --> 00:51:22.350
The 1st and 3rd Fleets will buy time
for the main force to raid the Solomon area:

00:51:22.350 --> 00:51:27.890
the battleships and night battle units
that make up the 2nd Fleet.

00:51:29.010 --> 00:51:37.130
The 2nd Fleet's main raid force will have
Hiei, Kirishima, and 1st BatDiv's Yamato.

00:51:37.130 --> 00:51:41.450
Jintsu's 2nd Desron will escort the force.

00:51:42.950 --> 00:51:48.140
Meanwhile, Sendai will lead the reinforced
3rd Desron and the advance recon squad,

00:51:48.140 --> 00:51:52.330
go ahead of the raid force,
and clear the path for them.

00:51:53.840 --> 00:51:56.410
The 1st, 2nd, and 3rd Fleets,

00:51:56.410 --> 00:51:59.420
and my fleet, the last line of defense.

00:51:59.420 --> 00:52:01.550
We'll have four fleets in this all-out war!

00:52:03.080 --> 00:52:05.010
I'm counting on all of you!

00:52:40.820 --> 00:52:45.180
The advance carrier battle group has reached
the South Pacific area of operations.

00:52:45.700 --> 00:52:47.740
Message from the flagship, Hiryu.

00:52:47.740 --> 00:52:50.350
"Recon aircraft have been deployed.

00:52:51.090 --> 00:52:54.320
Preparing to launch fighters."

00:52:54.320 --> 00:52:57.030
Message from Akagi of the main carrier group.

00:52:57.510 --> 00:52:59.070
"Yet to spot enemy.

00:52:59.070 --> 00:53:02.130
Sending out second batch of recon aircraft."

00:53:03.650 --> 00:53:05.450
Where's the enemy fleet?

00:53:05.450 --> 00:53:07.690
We're dangling such huge bait.

00:53:07.690 --> 00:53:09.710
They'll definitely bite.

00:53:09.710 --> 00:53:11.080
They have to.

00:53:11.080 --> 00:53:14.680
Otherwise, the raid force will be wiped out.

00:53:14.680 --> 00:53:15.800
Please...

00:53:31.910 --> 00:53:33.190
U-Um...

00:53:33.810 --> 00:53:35.620
What is it, 5th CarDiv?

00:53:36.160 --> 00:53:38.480
My second, Zuikaku, has a suggestion.

00:53:38.780 --> 00:53:40.280
U-Uh...

00:53:40.280 --> 00:53:43.240
"Recommend increasing escort aircraft."

00:53:50.240 --> 00:53:51.540
This is Akagi.

00:53:51.540 --> 00:53:54.280
I accept 5th CarDiv's suggestion.

00:53:54.280 --> 00:53:57.710
Each aircraft carrier is to
deploy further escort aircraft.

00:53:58.200 --> 00:54:00.680
Launch as soon as ready!

00:54:30.530 --> 00:54:31.610
Enemy spotted!

00:55:28.300 --> 00:55:29.720
Not on my watch!

00:55:45.520 --> 00:55:46.320
Zuikaku!

00:55:55.580 --> 00:55:57.790
Fire!

00:56:02.770 --> 00:56:05.830
Message to HQ and raid force!

00:56:05.830 --> 00:56:09.970
Successfully diverted enemy fleet northward!

00:56:10.900 --> 00:56:14.140
<i>The 2nd Fleet can enter Ironbottom Sound now.</i>

00:56:14.910 --> 00:56:15.740
<i>Fubuki!</i>

00:56:17.640 --> 00:56:20.490
Message from 3rd Fleet Flagship Hiryu.

00:56:20.490 --> 00:56:22.440
"Recon aircraft spotted enemy carrier group.

00:56:22.900 --> 00:56:29.360
2nd CarDiv's Hiryu and Soryu and
4th CarDiv's Ryujo deploying fighters en masse!"

00:56:29.730 --> 00:56:30.850
They did it.

00:56:32.280 --> 00:56:37.080
I hope we can get through this
and give them a taste of their own medicine!

00:56:37.080 --> 00:56:39.080
That would be nice.

00:56:41.350 --> 00:56:43.620
Give back...

00:56:44.690 --> 00:56:47.090
Give back...

00:56:49.270 --> 00:56:51.620
Give back...

00:57:01.070 --> 00:57:02.810
That was quicker than expected.

00:57:02.810 --> 00:57:05.240
Where's that radio message?

00:57:05.240 --> 00:57:07.790
Did the diversion to the north work or not?

00:57:07.790 --> 00:57:09.750
Give back...

00:57:12.150 --> 00:57:14.250
Give back...

00:57:22.770 --> 00:57:25.790
Advance squad has yet to encounter enemy.

00:57:26.840 --> 00:57:29.270
Given there haven't been any air raids yet,

00:57:29.270 --> 00:57:33.540
should we assume the enemy's carrier battle group
was successfully diverted northward?

00:57:35.550 --> 00:57:39.120
We would've received a message about that.

00:57:39.120 --> 00:57:40.470
But we haven't yet.

00:57:41.890 --> 00:57:44.350
Flagship, what will we do?

00:57:47.400 --> 00:57:50.230
We've entered Ironbottom Sound waters.

00:57:50.230 --> 00:57:52.840
The discoloration is increasing.

00:57:56.590 --> 00:57:57.740
What do we do?

00:57:58.380 --> 00:57:59.750
Let's keep going.

00:58:00.750 --> 00:58:02.290
Fubuki?

00:58:02.960 --> 00:58:04.780
I'm worried, too.

00:58:04.780 --> 00:58:07.200
But let's keep going.

00:58:07.200 --> 00:58:10.810
That's what we're here for.

00:58:12.810 --> 00:58:14.220
That's right.

00:58:14.220 --> 00:58:15.090
Hiei.

00:58:15.090 --> 00:58:16.250
I know.

00:58:16.250 --> 00:58:19.840
We will charge into Ironbottom Sound.

00:58:19.840 --> 00:58:22.350
Let the advance squad know!

00:58:22.660 --> 00:58:23.830
Roger that.

00:58:50.710 --> 00:58:52.050
Enemy spotted!

00:58:58.050 --> 00:58:59.260
Akatsuki!

00:59:01.970 --> 00:59:03.040
Ooi.

00:59:03.040 --> 00:59:04.150
Kitakami!

00:59:07.640 --> 00:59:09.370
See how you like this!

00:59:16.790 --> 00:59:18.460
Advance squad has encountered enemy!

00:59:18.460 --> 00:59:20.110
They're engaging them!

00:59:20.110 --> 00:59:21.570
Ready artiller—

00:59:22.390 --> 00:59:23.430
Hiei!

00:59:28.000 --> 00:59:29.820
New enemy battleships?

00:59:29.820 --> 00:59:31.090
Two of them?

00:59:31.540 --> 00:59:33.220
Damn you!

00:59:33.670 --> 00:59:34.750
Kirishima!

00:59:34.750 --> 00:59:35.730
Yes!

00:59:37.800 --> 00:59:39.660
Close-quarters night artillery battle!

00:59:39.660 --> 00:59:41.950
All ships, open concentrated fire!

00:59:50.370 --> 00:59:51.190
The equipment!

00:59:54.560 --> 00:59:55.820
Considerable damage!

00:59:55.820 --> 00:59:56.890
This isn't good!

00:59:57.860 --> 00:59:59.660
We knew that coming in!

00:59:59.660 --> 01:00:01.050
We have to hang in there!

01:00:01.900 --> 01:00:03.030
You'll be a sitting duck!

01:00:03.030 --> 01:00:05.030
It's fine! Here I go!

01:00:12.470 --> 01:00:14.410
Hiei, I see them.

01:00:14.410 --> 01:00:15.420
Thank you.

01:00:16.370 --> 01:00:20.820
Yamato, broadside battery,
loading armor piercing shells!

01:00:20.820 --> 01:00:22.090
Fire!

01:00:36.860 --> 01:00:37.870
Hey.

01:00:37.870 --> 01:00:39.530
Things are looking crazy over there.

01:00:44.720 --> 01:00:46.240
All ships, turn around!

01:00:46.240 --> 01:00:48.190
We'll go support the raid force!

01:00:48.190 --> 01:00:50.080
Hey, Sendai.

01:00:50.660 --> 01:00:51.640
Look at that.

01:00:56.670 --> 01:00:59.720
Crap, we've got visitors, too?

01:00:59.720 --> 01:01:00.940
Looks like it.

01:01:00.940 --> 01:01:03.050
Come, it's time for a night battle!

01:01:14.180 --> 01:01:15.060
Like that!

01:01:29.610 --> 01:01:31.870
Advance squad joining in.

01:01:32.450 --> 01:01:33.740
All right.

01:01:33.740 --> 01:01:37.540
Yamato will now take over as flagship.

01:01:37.540 --> 01:01:42.340
All ships are to follow Yamato's lead
and complete the mission.

01:01:43.220 --> 01:01:44.640
Hiei.

01:01:44.640 --> 01:01:45.930
She'll be fine.

01:01:48.900 --> 01:01:50.510
I'll be with her.

01:01:51.080 --> 01:01:54.740
Let's reshuffle around lightly damaged ships.

01:01:54.740 --> 01:01:56.100
Jintsu.

01:01:56.100 --> 01:01:58.160
Take care of these runts.

01:01:58.160 --> 01:01:59.030
Yeah, yeah.

01:01:59.030 --> 01:02:01.000
Sis, those wounds...

01:02:01.000 --> 01:02:03.020
Oh, I'm fine.

01:02:03.020 --> 01:02:04.590
They'll heal if I lick 'em.

01:02:04.590 --> 01:02:05.680
Ow...

01:02:06.680 --> 01:02:09.880
We shot all our torpedoes,

01:02:09.880 --> 01:02:11.870
so we'll escort the damaged ships back.

01:02:12.530 --> 01:02:13.770
Please do.

01:02:20.480 --> 01:02:23.080
The energetic ones went off, huh?

01:02:23.700 --> 01:02:29.310
Now, let's defend Hiei and the rest
and get back to Shortland Islands.

01:02:30.750 --> 01:02:32.010
Kitakami?

01:02:33.810 --> 01:02:36.650
Ooi, this might be bad.

01:02:40.060 --> 01:02:42.020
A new enemy fleet.

01:02:44.180 --> 01:02:46.410
This is, uh...

01:02:47.400 --> 01:02:48.730
Kirishima.

01:02:48.730 --> 01:02:50.160
I know.

01:02:57.170 --> 01:02:59.330
Gotta love nights.

01:02:59.330 --> 01:03:02.170
No better time to go.

01:03:29.990 --> 01:03:31.450
Like this!

01:03:37.690 --> 01:03:41.210
Go!

01:03:52.110 --> 01:03:54.010
What is that?

01:03:54.280 --> 01:03:55.720
Is that...

01:03:55.720 --> 01:03:58.930
The center of Ironbottom Sound.

01:04:11.820 --> 01:04:15.700
From here on in,
enemy attacks will likely grow fiercer.

01:04:15.700 --> 01:04:18.380
Heavily damaged ships are to fall back,

01:04:18.380 --> 01:04:21.330
and those remaining are to
prioritize reaching the target.

01:05:04.880 --> 01:05:07.000
Watch out, Fubuki!

01:05:16.680 --> 01:05:18.010
Yamato!

01:05:22.040 --> 01:05:25.290
I'm fine... I can still fight...

01:05:28.400 --> 01:05:30.280
Yamato!

01:05:43.660 --> 01:05:45.150
Mutsuki!

01:05:46.480 --> 01:05:47.920
Mutsuki...

01:06:30.540 --> 01:06:32.210
Kisaragi!

01:06:37.440 --> 01:06:40.260
Is that you, Kisaragi?

01:06:40.260 --> 01:06:42.760
Why are you here?

01:06:43.480 --> 01:06:45.770
I'm glad I made it in time.

01:06:50.680 --> 01:06:51.570
Mutsuki!

01:06:52.820 --> 01:06:54.020
Fubuki.

01:06:54.950 --> 01:06:57.990
You hear it, right?

01:06:59.160 --> 01:07:00.750
That voice.

01:07:00.750 --> 01:07:03.510
There's someone waiting for you.

01:07:03.510 --> 01:07:05.770
For me?

01:07:06.160 --> 01:07:08.170
I want to go back...

01:07:08.870 --> 01:07:10.780
I want to go back...

01:07:11.710 --> 01:07:13.460
Give back...

01:07:14.690 --> 01:07:16.900
Give back...

01:07:17.590 --> 01:07:19.300
Come to me...

01:07:20.230 --> 01:07:21.450
Fubuki.

01:07:23.810 --> 01:07:30.100
I was worried about what'd happen
if Kisaragi turned into an Abyssal Vessel.

01:07:32.520 --> 01:07:36.150
But she's still the Kisaragi I know!

01:07:42.240 --> 01:07:44.600
Go on, Fubuki.

01:07:45.950 --> 01:07:50.030
I am the first Yamato-Class Battleship.

01:07:50.030 --> 01:07:54.070
I won't be defeated by small fry.

01:08:09.160 --> 01:08:10.960
I'll be back!

01:08:10.960 --> 01:08:15.570
I'll confirm what's there—
who's there—and come back!

01:08:20.740 --> 01:08:22.410
I wish you luck!

01:10:25.720 --> 01:10:30.210
<i>Did I sink?</i>

01:10:31.480 --> 01:10:34.850
Endlessly repeated battles.

01:10:34.850 --> 01:10:39.560
Across eras, seas, and emotions,

01:10:40.000 --> 01:10:45.170
the regrets grow stronger with each cycle.

01:10:45.890 --> 01:10:46.880
Who are you?

01:10:46.880 --> 01:10:48.590
Savo Sound.

01:10:49.060 --> 01:10:51.690
Ironbottom Sound.

01:10:51.690 --> 01:10:55.000
Many ships have sunk here.

01:10:55.000 --> 01:10:59.500
And, first Special-Class Destroyer, Fubuki,

01:10:59.500 --> 01:11:00.970
you are one of them.

01:11:02.110 --> 01:11:09.310
Without displaying your "special" nature
or accomplishing what was expected of you,

01:11:09.310 --> 01:11:11.030
you sank, filled with regret.

01:11:11.470 --> 01:11:14.070
I sank?

01:11:14.070 --> 01:11:16.960
Yes, you sank here.

01:11:17.260 --> 01:11:21.380
And you will keep sinking here.

01:11:22.940 --> 01:11:26.380
But you didn't want to sink.

01:11:26.380 --> 01:11:29.510
You didn't want these waters to be the end.

01:11:29.870 --> 01:11:33.140
That's what you strongly wished for.

01:11:33.920 --> 01:11:36.070
The ocean with an iron bottom,

01:11:36.070 --> 01:11:39.060
and the regrets and desires lying there...

01:11:39.060 --> 01:11:41.440
They saved you,

01:11:41.440 --> 01:11:44.400
and they sank me.

01:11:44.400 --> 01:11:48.380
That's how you and I were born.

01:11:48.380 --> 01:11:51.490
You and I?

01:11:59.590 --> 01:12:00.680
That's right.

01:12:00.680 --> 01:12:06.750
And, within this endless circle of war,

01:12:06.750 --> 01:12:08.510
you became special.

01:12:09.350 --> 01:12:13.210
You lost all your sad memories,

01:12:13.210 --> 01:12:16.390
left me to rot at the bottom of the ocean,

01:12:16.390 --> 01:12:20.060
and became free.

01:12:20.060 --> 01:12:22.110
Curse you.

01:12:22.110 --> 01:12:26.700
Free from the shackles of an endless cycle.

01:12:26.700 --> 01:12:30.030
Instead of letting a sad fate chain you down,

01:12:30.030 --> 01:12:32.380
you live on the battlefield

01:12:32.380 --> 01:12:35.770
and alter the fates of Fleet Girls.

01:12:35.770 --> 01:12:37.190
Who, me?

01:12:38.040 --> 01:12:41.880
But that is unacceptable.

01:12:41.880 --> 01:12:46.280
We are beings meant to be
forgotten, glossed over,

01:12:46.280 --> 01:12:52.730
and disappear in a sad, everlasting cycle.

01:12:56.510 --> 01:12:58.040
Is that...?

01:13:00.690 --> 01:13:02.860
<i>I wanted to save them.</i>

01:13:05.540 --> 01:13:10.090
I split off from you as you gained freedom

01:13:10.090 --> 01:13:17.120
and was left with hate, envy,
and bloodthirst for those above the water...

01:13:17.120 --> 01:13:18.090
<i>I'm cold.</i>

01:13:18.090 --> 01:13:20.040
Nothing else.

01:13:20.720 --> 01:13:22.200
No...

01:13:22.200 --> 01:13:28.670
So I'll melt away everything on the surface.

01:13:28.670 --> 01:13:31.000
I hate them, after all.

01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:32.970
Deep down,

01:13:32.970 --> 01:13:36.460
you wanted to come back, too, right?

01:13:36.460 --> 01:13:38.890
To this graveyard of metal?

01:13:39.290 --> 01:13:40.560
Welcome home.

01:13:42.980 --> 01:13:44.170
<i>So dark.</i>

01:13:45.380 --> 01:13:46.520
It's all right now.

01:13:46.520 --> 01:13:47.400
<i>Take care.</i>

01:13:47.400 --> 01:13:49.610
Let's fade away into this ocean together.

01:13:50.260 --> 01:13:52.150
You don't have to work hard.

01:13:52.150 --> 01:13:54.900
You don't have to make any progress.

01:13:55.240 --> 01:13:59.320
Let's just stay broken in an endless despair.

01:13:59.320 --> 01:14:01.990
Let's vanish into a closed world.

01:14:02.580 --> 01:14:11.630
And let's wait here for the tragedy
that is bound to start over one day.

01:14:23.780 --> 01:14:26.200
Just disappear!

01:14:26.200 --> 01:14:29.480
Isn't that why you came back here?!

01:14:29.480 --> 01:14:34.010
Come back and sink here over and over!

01:14:34.010 --> 01:14:38.750
In this seabed devoid of light or promise.

01:14:38.750 --> 01:14:42.680
And, with everyone forgetting about you,

01:14:42.680 --> 01:14:44.500
just disappear.

01:14:45.750 --> 01:14:47.870
No... That's too...

01:14:50.540 --> 01:14:52.680
I don't want to...

01:15:18.740 --> 01:15:20.380
<i>I couldn't protect them.</i>

01:15:19.020 --> 01:15:20.370
<i>It hurt.</i>

01:15:19.540 --> 01:15:21.620
I wanted to save them.

01:15:20.370 --> 01:15:22.080
<i>I wanted to protect them.</i>

01:15:20.770 --> 01:15:21.620
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

01:15:21.620 --> 01:15:22.760
<i>Help me.</i>

01:15:22.080 --> 01:15:24.080
<i>I couldn't save them.</i>

01:15:22.760 --> 01:15:25.110
I'm sinking.

01:15:24.080 --> 01:15:27.240
<i>I couldn't make it.</i>

01:15:24.560 --> 01:15:26.180
<i>I wanted to make it so badly.</i>

01:15:26.630 --> 01:15:28.160
<i>I wanted to make it so badly.</i>

01:15:28.160 --> 01:15:29.830
Come here.

01:15:29.830 --> 01:15:31.300
Come to me.

01:15:31.750 --> 01:15:32.940
Sink.

01:15:32.940 --> 01:15:34.170
<i>Take care.</i>

01:15:34.170 --> 01:15:35.630
Sink.

01:15:35.630 --> 01:15:37.050
<i>Don't forget me.</i>

01:15:38.130 --> 01:15:39.560
<i>Goodbye.</i>

01:15:42.370 --> 01:15:43.720
<i>I see.</i>

01:15:44.640 --> 01:15:47.230
<i>I'm a symbol of hope.</i>

01:15:48.600 --> 01:15:53.610
<i>A symbol of hope
created by all of their desires.</i>

01:15:54.500 --> 01:15:56.070
<i>Not regret,</i>

01:15:56.910 --> 01:15:58.420
<i>but hope!</i>

01:15:59.430 --> 01:16:01.640
<i>Hope to get through this war</i>

01:16:02.530 --> 01:16:05.870
<i>and take a step forward.</i>

01:16:25.080 --> 01:16:28.380
There's nothing wrong with change.

01:16:33.390 --> 01:16:34.410
Stay away.

01:16:35.310 --> 01:16:37.690
It doesn't have to be an endless cycle.

01:16:37.690 --> 01:16:40.190
We don't have to stay here.

01:16:40.820 --> 01:16:42.240
It's all right.

01:16:42.740 --> 01:16:45.560
Don't come any closer... Stay away!

01:16:45.560 --> 01:16:51.410
It's okay if we go back to the surface
and take a step forward into a new world.

01:16:51.840 --> 01:16:54.580
No... If I did that...

01:16:58.960 --> 01:17:02.220
Don't worry. Everyone's there for us.

01:17:02.490 --> 01:17:04.760
No... No!

01:17:30.080 --> 01:17:31.790
Their desires live strong.

01:17:31.790 --> 01:17:35.170
As strong as their regrets may be,
their hope's just as strong.

01:17:35.860 --> 01:17:39.180
It'll be fine. I'm sure they'll remember.

01:17:39.180 --> 01:17:42.830
I won't forget you, either.

01:17:42.830 --> 01:17:45.340
We can move forward!

01:17:45.870 --> 01:17:46.980
So please...

01:18:32.920 --> 01:18:34.020
What's going on?

01:18:35.060 --> 01:18:36.380
Kisaragi!

01:18:49.660 --> 01:18:50.890
Kisaragi!

01:18:57.760 --> 01:18:59.290
Kisaragi.

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:03.260
Mutsuki...

01:19:03.780 --> 01:19:05.340
I'm so sorry.

01:19:05.790 --> 01:19:08.430
No, why?

01:19:08.850 --> 01:19:16.120
I didn't want to fight you and the rest.

01:19:16.120 --> 01:19:19.350
I know! We all know that!

01:19:19.350 --> 01:19:22.360
I didn't want to hurt you.

01:19:22.360 --> 01:19:25.070
I couldn't come back, though.

01:19:25.490 --> 01:19:29.160
No... This can't happen!

01:19:30.500 --> 01:19:32.410
But you know what?

01:19:32.990 --> 01:19:35.690
Don't worry. You'll be fine.

01:19:36.370 --> 01:19:38.250
If you can just dock...

01:19:39.680 --> 01:19:42.920
Mutsuki, you know...

01:19:43.750 --> 01:19:46.170
The time we spent together,

01:19:46.170 --> 01:19:49.410
the warmth we shared,

01:19:49.410 --> 01:19:51.590
and your voice...

01:19:52.130 --> 01:19:56.950
I want to go before I forget it all.

01:20:03.140 --> 01:20:09.900
I wanted to say goodbye this time.

01:20:21.590 --> 01:20:24.230
We'll always be together.

01:20:25.630 --> 01:20:29.350
Let's meet again, no matter what.

01:20:29.780 --> 01:20:34.180
I swear I'll find you.

01:20:34.180 --> 01:20:35.240
So...

01:20:35.760 --> 01:20:39.230
Don't forget about me, okay?

01:20:40.580 --> 01:20:48.940
Let me hear the rest of your story then.

01:20:55.270 --> 01:20:57.300
It's a promise, okay?

01:22:00.720 --> 01:22:02.220
Welcome back.

01:22:02.220 --> 01:22:03.680
You did well.

01:22:08.020 --> 01:22:10.780
Welcome back, Fubuki.

01:22:23.380 --> 01:22:24.500
The ocean...

01:22:35.840 --> 01:22:37.930
Like, hey!

01:23:06.850 --> 01:23:07.790
There.

01:23:08.480 --> 01:23:10.460
I'll be going now.

01:23:10.920 --> 01:23:11.830
Okay.

01:23:13.620 --> 01:23:15.130
Here's your lunch.

01:23:15.130 --> 01:23:16.430
Do your best.

01:23:16.430 --> 01:23:18.930
Wow, thanks!

01:23:18.930 --> 01:23:21.350
I'm off, then!

01:23:21.350 --> 01:23:23.570
Take care!

01:23:27.680 --> 01:23:29.930
Hey, Yudachi!

01:23:29.930 --> 01:23:32.230
Mind your manners!

01:23:39.410 --> 01:23:42.410
New 2nd Fleet, start up!

01:23:43.220 --> 01:23:45.630
Vanguard, 2nd Torpedo Squadron,

01:23:45.630 --> 01:23:46.750
prepare to weigh anchor!

01:23:51.330 --> 01:23:53.040
Don't worry.

01:23:53.040 --> 01:23:59.180
I'll bring peace back to the oceans someday.

01:23:59.600 --> 01:24:00.680
I promise.

01:24:01.570 --> 01:24:03.410
2nd Torpedo Squadron,

01:24:03.410 --> 01:24:05.150
11th Destroyer Division,

01:24:05.150 --> 01:24:05.970
weigh anchor.

01:24:06.850 --> 01:24:08.490
2nd Torpedo Squadron,

01:24:08.490 --> 01:24:10.030
11th Destroyer Division,

01:24:10.030 --> 01:24:12.730
First Special-Class Destroyer, Fubuki!

01:24:13.610 --> 01:24:15.240
Weighing anchor!
